WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.062
Let’s walk through Timeline.

00:00:02.062 --> 00:00:05.162
Use chronology to test sequence, identify gaps, and

00:00:05.162 --> 00:00:07.350
avoid duplicate interpretation.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.025
The timeline explains how the session developed;

00:00:10.025 --> 00:00:14.000
the owning artifact remains authoritative for current workflow state.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.212
On this slide, review the chronological session record and

00:00:17.212 --> 00:00:20.512
the structured snapshots published by manual saves.

00:00:20.512 --> 00:00:23.613
In practice, use the timeline to check sequence,

00:00:23.613 --> 00:00:27.950
identify gaps, and avoid duplicating an observation already captured

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:28.113
.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:31.460
When you are ready, use Open Timeline to move

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.947
to the live surface.

00:00:32.947 --> 00:00:35.660
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:35.810
.
